      "content": "That seems like a pretty one-sided view. You're basically saying that any economic disruption caused by strict enforcement is just \"necessary,\" but you aren't really acknowledging the arguments from economists who say that losing that labor pool could cause food prices to spike or lead to industry collapses. Isn't it more accurate to say that the net economic effect is actually a huge debate rather than just a \"necessary evil\"?",
